  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Stoat
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 14
  entries:
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Field Dipole
    AbilityDescription: 'Squeeze a trigger and a sink-source pair (a black hole and
      a white hole, joined as a wormhole) is laid 250 u ahead, the poles together,
      in the frame you had then. The triggers'' DIFFERENCE pulls the poles apart
      sideways - the sink on the deeper trigger''s side - and their SUM pulls them
      apart lengthways, the sink always the nearer: one trigger alone gives a slight
      diagonal, both buried put the sink dead ahead and the source 120 u beyond it.
      Ease off and the poles come back together; let go of both and they meet and
      annihilate, so there is only ever one pair. The poles'' strength and size are
      fixed - only the separation (the dipole moment) follows the triggers. The field
      bends your flight and anything that crosses the sink''s horizon goes through
      it: you come out of the source; a rival vessel comes out stripped of its
      crystals, left on the sink''s side; a creature is swallowed (killed); a prism
      vanishes. Space is size: both poles'' horizon and pull scale x1 -> x2 at level
      10 (StoatDipoleConfigSO.poleSize, read live). R_VesselActions/STOAT_DIPOLE.md.'
    Input: 2
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Theft
    UpgradeDescription: 'Prisms the sink swallows are STOLEN instead of destroyed:
      they come out of the source in your domain (Prism.Steal, a super-steal - a
      shield is no answer to a horizon). Gated on IsUpgradeActive(Space), replicated,
      so every peer''s copy of the pair steals the same prisms.'
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Pathfinder
    AbilityDescription: 'Passive. The path your hull will fly on the inputs you hold
      right now, run 600 u ahead through your dipole''s field and drawn as dots from
      the nose (blue-grey). When your poles WARP that path at all - it bends 3 degrees
      or more, or it goes through the wormhole - it turns lime and you fly down it
      faster: a warp of the hull''s own flight clock, so the path stays the path and
      only arrives sooner. Time is rate: the boost is x2 at rest, x3 at level 5, x4 at
      level 10 (StoatDipoleConfigSO.boost, read live). The base turn rates are x0.4
      (pitch / yaw 48, roll 52), so the hull leans on its poles to turn.
      X still holds the hull still (the Sparrow''s stop), outside the four abilities.'
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: ''
    UpgradeDescription: 'OPEN DESIGN SLOT - proposals in Docs/ElementalAbilitySystem/FLEET_MAPS.md
      (Stoat), not implemented.'
